# Runner trigger/result files. These change on every runner invocation and
# have no business in source control — a permanently-dirty tree here produced
# constant "UNCOMMITTED in cirrus-repo" noise in session-wrap, which is exactly
# what masked three genuinely untracked modules on 2026-08-19 (S69).
.run-command
.run-result

# transient deploy trigger — written by Cowork, consumed and removed by
# cowork-deploy.sh. Committing it produces a spurious add/delete pair (S71).
.deploy-job

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# S79 (2026-08-26) — the untracked-path backlog that has been threatening every
# deploy since S70.
#
# `git pull --ff-only` aborts when an incoming commit adds a path that already
# exists UNTRACKED on the box. That is the S70 failure: CIRRUS silently refused
# every pull for days while `deploy` reported success. deploy-drift has warned
# "20+ modified/untracked path(s)" on BOTH boxes ever since, and it sat on
# carry-over untouched because the check named a count and never the paths.
#
# Nothing below is deleted — ignoring a file only changes git's view of it, and
# git will cleanly overwrite an IGNORED path during a merge instead of aborting.
# That is exactly the property we need.
#
# Everything here was checked before being listed: each is either generated at
# runtime, a backup, build output, per-box config, or a Cowork-owned script that
# has no business in this repo.

# Backups and pre-change snapshots. Every *.bak-<date> under config/ came from
# a tool that rewrites a config in place, plus a few hand-made ones.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.pre-*

# Virtualenv (CUMULUS builds its own; it is not source).
.venv/

# Build/report output. A bare `out/` matches at any depth, which covers
# newdev/out/, hoa_leads/out/ and snowbrief/out/ as well as the top-level one.
out/
bench/
newdev/*.xlsx
property-management/

# Stray logs outside logs/ (that directory is already ignored above).
*.log

# Per-box RUNTIME state, same reasoning as intake_state.json above — each box
# owns its own copy and committing one would overwrite the other's.
#   topics-pedagogy.json  is CREATED by intake.py from client requests
#   vendor_mail_ledger.json / cookie_watchlist.json are ledgers written by jobs
#   pedagogy_state.json    is a per-box cursor
config/topics-pedagogy.json
config/pedagogy_state.json
config/vendor_mail_ledger.json
config/cookie_watchlist.json

# Per-box provisioning, deliberately NOT shared: cumulus-status checks that this
# exists on the box, and the two boxes hold different values.
provision/platform.env

# Cowork-owned scripts that get copied onto the boxes by the credential
# tooling. They live in ~/Documents/Cowork/runner/ and are versioned THERE;
# a copy on the box is a deployment artefact, not source for this repo.
apply_creds_encrypted.py
creds_crypto.py
materialize_credentials.sh
materialize_credentials_cirrus.sh
deploy-cirrus.sh

# One-off experiments left on CUMULUS. Ignored rather than deleted — they are
# somebody's working notes, and this file's job is to unblock deploys, not to
# decide what is worth keeping.
apify_*.py
x_scan.py

# Referenced by nothing in the tree; a leftover next to the real sources.json.
cirrus-digest-sources.json

# S79 — match the FAMILY, not the suffixes that happened to exist today.
# The *.bak-* / *.pre-* patterns above covered the copies present on 2026-08-26
# and would NOT have caught `credentials.json.save`, which lived on CIRRUS until
# S63 and still sits in the Mac's backup store. Buddy's requirement is that
# these never reach the internet; a rule that enumerates known suffixes is the
# wrong shape for that (same lesson as T36). Nothing plaintext has ever been
# committed in this repo's history — this keeps it that way by construction.
# credentials.template.json does not match this pattern and stays tracked.
credentials.json.*
